# Test: a VPP worker core outside the kernel's isolated set is reported
# Spec: spec-vpp-isolated-cpus AC-5 (closed 2026-09-07)
# VALIDATES: `ze doctor --json` reports doctor-vpp-cpu-isolation when the worker
#            cores VPP is pinned to are online but were never isolated, so the
#            Linux scheduler still places work on them.
# PREVENTS: the silent case this spec exists to remove -- a busy-polling VPP
#           worker competing with every other runnable task on its CPU, with
#           nothing telling the operator.
#
# Its own file because an expect=stdout: assertion is FILE-level: the runner
# checks it against the concatenated output of every command in the file
# (runner_exec.go, rec.ClientOutput). The positive case here and the negative
# case in test/plugin/vpp-isolated-cpus.ci are contradictory statements about
# one string, so they cannot share a file.
#
# Linux-only: the fixture stands in for /sys/devices/system/cpu, and the doctor
# check is Linux-tagged. The fixture host has eight CPUs and isolated 2-4.

option=skip-os:value=aix,android,darwin,dragonfly,freebsd,illumos,ios,js,netbsd,openbsd,plan9,solaris,wasip1,windows
option=env:var=ze.test.vpp.cpu.root:value=cpufix
# The hugepage check shares this report. Its root is redirected to a directory
# that does not exist, so it reports one error and the exit code below is a fact
# about the fixture rather than about the machine running the test.
option=env:var=ze.test.doctor.hugepages-root:value=nohugepages

tmpfs=cpufix/online:terminator=EOF_ON
0-7
EOF_ON

tmpfs=cpufix/isolated:terminator=EOF_ISO
2-4
EOF_ISO

tmpfs=shared-workers.conf:terminator=EOF_SHARED
vpp {
	enabled true;
	cpu {
		main-core 0;
		worker-cores 6-7;
	}
}
EOF_SHARED

# AC-5: cores 6 and 7 are online but were never isolated, so the operator is
# told the Linux scheduler still places work on them.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json shared-workers.conf:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-vpp-cpu-isolation
expect=stdout:contains=worker core 6-7 is not isolated
